WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.178
Caroline Aghajanian: Taylor
Guitars was founded by

00:00:13.178 --> 00:00:16.735
Bob Taylor and Kurt Listug in 1974.

00:00:16.735 --> 00:00:19.402
That's fairly new considering
some of its competitors,

00:00:19.402 --> 00:00:22.170
like Gibson or Martin Guitars.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:24.660
Today, big music names like Taylor Swift,

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.865
Jason Mraz, and Zac Brown

00:00:26.865 --> 00:00:30.051
strum to the tune of a Taylor guitar.

00:00:30.051 --> 00:00:31.300
Hi, I'm Caroline,

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:32.720
and today we're taking you inside

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.120
the Taylor Guitars factory,

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.950
where they combine
craftsmanship and automation

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:39.233
to produce hundreds of guitars a day.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:44.397
The company has two factories.

00:00:44.397 --> 00:00:45.960
One in El Cajon, California,

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.170
and the other in Tecate, Mexico.

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:53.170
In 2017, they made over
$102 million in revenue.

00:00:53.852 --> 00:00:56.362
Chris Wellons: Currently, we're
producing over 720 guitars

00:00:56.362 --> 00:00:58.330
a day between both of our factories.

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:02.472
We're slated to build over
160,000 guitars this year alone.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:08.386
Caroline: Taylor guitars
range between $350

00:01:08.386 --> 00:01:10.520
to more than $9,000.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:12.143
So, why such a high price tag?

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.780
Well, a big factor is the type of wood

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.520
and materials used.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.810
They currently have over
35 species of wood in house

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:22.140
to choose from.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:23.460
Their factory in El Cajon

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:26.050
makes their guitars out of all solid wood

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:28.233
instead of laminate construction.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.756
Some models require advanced
woodworking techniques

00:01:34.756 --> 00:01:36.970
or greater decorated detail work,

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:39.095
which can also increase the price.

00:01:45.622 --> 00:01:47.579
If the guitar is well maintained,

00:01:47.579 --> 00:01:49.360
the sound will continue to improve

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.490
as the guitar's wood ages,

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:54.431
making it sound richer and more resonant.

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:00.050
The factory runs 24 hours a day,

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.408
five days a week.

00:02:01.408 --> 00:02:04.140
They have over 900
employees building guitars

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.505
with the help of some robotics.

00:02:06.505 --> 00:02:08.620
Chris: We blend robotics and automation

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:10.112
with lots of handwork.

00:02:10.112 --> 00:02:12.357
I think automation is
great, first and foremost.

00:02:12.357 --> 00:02:15.000
It's very important to
continue to advance the factory

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.100
and move it forward.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.690
The one thing we pride ourselves on

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:20.597
is we've never replaced an
employee with any automation.

00:02:20.597 --> 00:02:23.161
We've always deployed those
employees into other areas

00:02:23.161 --> 00:02:24.410
or into the same department,

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.019
which has allowed us to increase
our production capacities.

